{"id":88097,"title":"PDF State of the Art in Procedural Noise Functions","url":"https://www-sop.inria.fr/reves/Basilic/2010/LLCDDELPZ10/LLCDDELPZ10STARPNF.pdf","final_url":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260708100910/https://www-sop.inria.fr/reves/Basilic/2010/LLCDDELPZ10/LLCDDELPZ10STARPNF.pdf","year":null,"kind":"web","source":"ddg","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":null,"ctype":null,"text_src":"wayback","fetched_at":1793149225.0418477,"text_chars":93228,"abstract":"www-sop.inria.fr\n\nhttps://www-sop.inria.fr › reves › Basilic › 2010 › LLCDDELPZ10 › LLCDDELPZ10STARPNF.pdf\n\nPDF State of the Art in Procedural Noise Functions\nAbstract Procedural noise functions are widely used in Computer Graphics, from off-line rendering in movie production to interactive video games. The ability to add complex and intricate details at low memory and authoring cost is one of its main attractions. This state-of-the-art report is motivated by the inherent importance of noise in graphics, the widespread use of noise in industry, and ...","file":null,"marks":[],"links":["http://web.archive.org/web/20260708100910/https://www-sop.inria.fr/reves/Basilic/2010/LLCDDELPZ10/LLCDDELPZ10STARPNF.pdf","https://www-sop.inria.fr/reves/Basilic/2010/LLCDDELPZ10/LLCDDELPZ10STARPNF.pdf"],"cited_by":[{"path":"978-simplex-noise.md","name":"Simplex Noise","k":11},{"path":"4211-perlin-noise-2d.md","name":"Perlin Noise 2D","k":7},{"path":"4253-fractal-brownian-motion-fbm-with-perlin-noise.md","name":"Fractal Brownian Motion (fBm) with Perlin Noise","k":7},{"path":"16450-anisotropic-noise.md","name":"Anisotropic Noise","k":3},{"path":"16451-fourier-spectral-synthesis.md","name":"Fourier Spectral Synthesis","k":3},{"path":"16469-gaussian-texture-filtering-via-jacobian-back-projection.md","name":"Gaussian Texture Filtering via Jacobian Back-projection","k":2},{"path":"16556-gabor-noise-surface-filtering.md","name":"Gabor Noise Surface Filtering","k":3},{"path":"16935-midpoint-displacement-fractal.md","name":"M